{
  "title": "Bride Poured Coffee Over Her Future Mother-in-Law's Head—Unaware She Paid for the Whole Wedding",
  "description": "She asked a stranger for a chair five weeks after heart surgery. The stranger was about to become her daughter-in-law.<br><br>Lucia Moreno, 58, started out selling coffee from a cart in San Antonio&apos;s Market Square. On a hotel terrace by the River Walk, she asked to borrow an empty chair. Vanessa Beaumont didn&apos;t even look up: &quot;Go sit on the curb.&quot; Then she poured her latte over Lucia&apos;s head while her parents laughed. Seconds later, a text lit up Lucia&apos;s phone: the wedding was paid in full, $310,000. Congratulations, mother of the groom. The only person who stood up for her, a waitress named Maya, was fired on the spot.<br><br>Lucia said nothing. She wanted to see who her son was really marrying. When the bride finally learned who she was, the tears came fast and the stories didn&apos;t match. Then her name disappeared from the wedding invitations, the bride&apos;s father told her, &quot;You pay, and you keep quiet,&quot; and on the wedding day the woman who paid for every flower was led to the last row: &quot;No coffee sellers in my photos.&quot;<br><br>👉 Watch till the end — the wedding is only the beginning, and the Beaumonts have one more move planned.<br><br>If you love stories where the people who look down on others finally face what they did, subscribe for a new story every week.<br><br>This is a fictional story made for entertainment. All characters, places and events are invented.<br><br><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/weddingdrama\">#WeddingDrama</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/karma\">#Karma</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/story\">#Story</a>",
